---
import translations from "@utils/t.ts";
import Layout from "@layouts/Layout.astro";
import Container from "@src/components/Container.astro";
import WorkoutsNav from "@src/components/WorkoutsNav.astro";

const t = translations(Astro.url);
---

<Layout title="Workouts" description="My workout routine.">
	<Container class="pt-16">
		<div class="text-center">
			<h1 class="mb-4 text-3xl font-semibold">Workouts</h1>
		</div>
		<WorkoutsNav />
		<div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
			<div class="text-center">
				<p>
					<a target="_blank" href="https://github.com/Andrew-Chen-Wang/blog/commits/main/src/pages/workouts/index.astro">
						Edit History
					</a>
				</p>
			</div>
			<p set:html={t.workouts_description} />

			<p>Here is my current workout regiment:</p>

			<h3>Pull Ups</h3>
			<p>Current PR, full extension, pronated: 10</p>
			<p>
				Down days: usually PR 1-2 times, then 4 more sets. Pull/push days: usually PR 1 time, then 2-5 more sets at PR-0/1, then PR-2, etc. I usually do 20-30 minutes for pull up training on Wednesday, Saturday, and Sunday with a single set bicep curl workout 1x5-10.
			</p>
			<p><a href="/workouts/pull-ups/">Pull-up progress</a></p>

			<h2>Day 1/Monday &ndash; Push (Strength)</h2>
			<p>Chest &bull; Shoulders &bull; Triceps &bull; Core</p>
			<div class="overflow-x-auto">
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th>Exercise</th>
							<th>Sets</th>
							<th>Current Weight (per arm; lvl 3 = 30 degrees on bench)</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<td>Seated Overhead Press</td>
							<td>3&times;10</td>
							<td>50 lb per arm</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Bench Press</td>
							<td>3&times;10</td>
							<td>60 lb per arm</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Hammer Press</td>
							<td>3&times;10&ndash;12</td>
							<td>50 lb per arm</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Push-ups</td>
							<td>2&times;30</td>
							<td>Bodyweight</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Triceps Pushdowns</td>
							<td>3&times;12&ndash;15</td>
							<td>62.5 lb</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Dumbbell Lateral Raises</td>
							<td>4&times;15</td>
							<td>30 lb per arm</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Leg Raises</td>
							<td>
								4 &times; 15
							</td>
							<td>Bodyweight</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p>Purpose: Heavy pressing and chest strength.</p>

			<h2>Day 2/Tuesday &ndash; Pull (Strength)</h2>
			<p>Back &bull; Biceps &bull; Core</p>
			<div class="overflow-x-auto">
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th>Exercise</th>
							<th>Sets</th>
							<th>Current Weight</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<td>Bicep Curls</td>
							<td>3&times;10</td>
							<td>40 lb per arm</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Pull Ups</td>
							<td>1-3&times;Failure</td>
							<td>Reach PR (currently 10)</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Row</td>
							<td>4&times;10</td>
							<td>127.5-135 lb</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Lat Pulldown</td>
							<td>4 sets</td>
							<td>127.5-135 lb pulldown (10x)</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Face Pulls</td>
							<td>4&times;15</td>
							<td>49-50.5 lb</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Cable Rear Delt Fly</td>
							<td>3&times;15</td>
							<td>17.5 lb</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Cable Crunch</td>
							<td>3&times;45&ndash;12</td>
							<td>72.5 lb</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p>Purpose: Pulling strength, posture, shoulder health.</p>

			<h2>Day 3/Thursday &ndash; Push (Volume)</h2>
			<p>Chest &bull; Shoulders &bull; Triceps &bull; Core</p>
			<div class="overflow-x-auto">
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th>Exercise</th>
							<th>Sets</th>
							<th>Current Weight</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<td>Incline Bench</td>
							<td>3&times;12</td>
							<td>60 lb (3rd level) per arm</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Cable fly</td>
							<td>3&times;10</td>
							<td>32.5 lb per arm</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Push-ups</td>
							<td>2&times;30</td>
							<td>Bodyweight</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Triceps Pushdowns or Dips</td>
							<td>3&times;12&ndash;15</td>
							<td>57.5 lb</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Dumbbell Lateral Raises</td>
							<td>4&times;15</td>
							<td>30 lb per arm</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Cable Crunch</td>
							<td>4&times;12</td>
							<td>72.5 lb (Level 4)</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p>
				Purpose: Upper chest, shoulder development, higher-volume
				pressing.
			</p>

			<h2>Day 4/Friday &ndash; Pull (Volume)</h2>
			<p>Back &bull; Biceps &bull; Core</p>
			<div class="overflow-x-auto">
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th>Exercise</th>
							<th>Sets</th>
							<th>Current Weight</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<td>Chest-Supported Row</td>
							<td>3&times;12</td>
							<td>40 lb (3rd level) per arm</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Lat Pulldown</td>
							<td>3&times;12</td>
							<td>127.5-135lb lb</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Face Pulls</td>
							<td>3&times;15</td>
							<td>49-50.5 lb</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Cable Rear Delt Fly</td>
							<td>3&times;15</td>
							<td>17.5 lb</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Bicep Curls</td>
							<td>3&times;12</td>
							<td>40 lb per arm</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Hanging leg raises</td>
							<td>4&times;12</td>
							<td>Bodyweight</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p>Purpose: Back thickness, posture, trunk stability.</p>

			<p>
				I started March/April 2025, stopped September to April 2026 (sporadically went maybe at most twice a week). I properly started up again around the beginning of April, and I tested between 3 or 4 days. 4 days seem to fit me much better since 3 days gave me the feeling of too much rejuvenation. Each workout takes 1-1.25 hours depending on my energy and amount of distraction.
			</p>

			<p>
				That&rsquo;s my current workout regiment, why I do it, how I
				feel, my goals, and how much longer I can continue. This is a living
				document, so I'll cut down on words, re-organize sections to be a more
				coherent story, and update this page with current weight numbers to
				have a record of progress and show people how long it takes to grow
				(with probably not enough protein). You can view the updated weight history using the <a target="_blank" href="https://github.com/Andrew-Chen-Wang/blog/commits/main/src/pages/workouts/index.astro">git history</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</Container>
</Layout>
